---
description: Guidelines for building RSpec tests in this repo
alwaysApply: true
---

- **Testing Approach**: Unit and integration tests can only be built in RSpec
- **Atomic Testing**: Tests must center on single discrete, deterministic behaviors
- **Discrete Testing**: Tests must not unecessarily duplicate testing the same behaviors
- **Testing Data**: ActiveRecord objects should not be created in the database without using FactoryBot
- **Factory Usage**: Prefer the `build` method in FactoryBot to `create` where possible to speed up test setup and teardown
- **External Service Testing**: Do not implement any automated tests that exectute a live to an external API service.
- **Anthropic SDK Testing**: Do not implement any automated tests that execute a live call to the Anthropic SDK or any outside services. Prefer mocking the response as defined in the [Anthropic Ruby SDK Docs](https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/cli-sdks-libraries/sdks/ruby)
- **Diagnostic request specs**: Request specs for the diagnostic submission endpoint must stub `DiagnosticService` and must not construct a live Anthropic client.
